<ontology/use_pharmaceuticals/use_pharmaceuticals__0750__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 27" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n27> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cream of Tartar used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 27"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "ARGOL: an acidulous concreto salt, the crust or sediment of wine vats and casks, which when purified is denominated cream of tartar; it is white or red, according to the wine of which it is the deposit, and largely used in medicine and the arts; also a Tartar name for the dried excrements of animals moulded into cakes and sold as fuel."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
